A||N||9||Elenor84||Performance Chip||||1||
Z||000000||Elenor84||01-28-2001||06:42 AM||||Hey guys...uknow on somne of the newer vehichles u can just throw in a computer chip and u get more hp?  Is that possible for fiero's?  Thx!<P>------------------<BR>Lance<BR>Click Image to go to site.<BR><A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/_XMCM/lancegspage/Index.html" TARGET=_blank><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sideview.jpg">  </A>||||reg||1
Z||000001||TheFiero64||01-28-2001||11:06 AM||||It is possible. The Fiero ECM(Computer) has a removable prom chip. The only problem is that they only make high performance chips for the V6 Fieros. There may be a custom chip programmer out there that can burn you a chip to change some parameters for more performance but, I have not seen any yet.<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>88 Coupe V6<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||10
Z||000002||terryk||01-28-2001||11:48 AM||||Other than changing calibrations to adjust for engine mods, there isn't much (if any) power to be found through a chip change. <P>Yes, if you run 92+ gas you can add more spark and maybe lean it out some and get a bit more power, but GM does a good job of tuning their chips. GM doesn't hide power (except in the turbo'd cars since the turbo will put out far more boost than the engine hand handle).<P>TK<BR> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||87GT||01-28-2001||12:26 PM||||I had a hypertech chip in my GT and recently decided to put the stock chip back in to see if there was any noticeable difference and I couldnt tell any change at all. It was a waste of money and having that chip only makes it eat more gas. hehehe||||reg||1
Z||000004||terryk||01-28-2001||12:35 PM||||If anyone has a spare performance chip, send it to me and I will see what they changed. I'll return it. The ones I looked at were useless.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Bruce||01-28-2001||12:40 PM||||As soon as I find my stock chip in storage, I'll send it to you. I think I was a sucker to buy the "performance" chip.||||reg||1
Z||000006||terryk||01-28-2001||12:59 PM||||I guess I should add a disclaimer here. I'm not making a sweeping statement that all of the chips are no good, but so far, none of them did much of anything and when I looked, I could see why. There very well might be some good ones out there. Well, there seems to be one..... ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Raydar||01-28-2001||01:57 PM||||When I had my 88 Firebird (305 TBI), I installed a Hypertech chip. They recommended installing a 160* thermostat, as well. I installed the thermostat first, then did the chip a few weeks later. The thermostat made a difference. The chip didn't.<BR>Save your money, unless you have a highly modded engine. Then have one custom made for your combo. <BR>Just my $.02.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe||||reg||1
Z||000008||theogre||01-28-2001||02:54 PM||||I have to agree with Terry. I've yet to see enough improvment from a chip in an OBDI GM computer to make it worth the trouble and cost to install it. Modifications to OBDII computers usually only help if the engine or transmission have been altered. (OBDII computers are really crabby about even small changes to the powertrain.)[All Stock Fiero computers are OBDI]<P>With help from a couple people I've been working on some things for the 4 cyl but this is only to change things like Fan turn on in the DIS motor and fix specific problems. I don't expect there is any performance to be had. I'm interested in seeing if the idle can be smoothed out some and eliminating a ping problem in the early DIS programming.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 01-28-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||Sleeper||01-28-2001||07:24 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by terryk:<BR>[BThe ones I looked at were useless.[/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>did you try the performance chip from J.E.T cuz i do feel a differance with my 85gt(it does suck up more gas but there is more power in the mid rpm's), though i think my chip is customize in a way cuz i ordered directly from J.E.T and they did some special sh*t to it, it was my 2nd one. <BR>||||reg||1
